{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.closed_form_trefoil_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.closed_form_trefoil_right","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/JonesPolynomial.lean#L104-L104","doc":"Trefoil 3_1 (right-handed): `QOU.KnotTheory.trefoil`, the closed\nbraid `σ_0^3` in `B_2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.closed_form_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.closed_form_unknot","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/JonesPolynomial.lean#L101-L101","doc":"`jonesAt (unknot, q) = 1` for all q.  Normalisation convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/JonesPolynomial.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.JonesPolynomialDef","kind":"class","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/JonesPolynomial.lean#L87-L105","doc":"**§3b-cond conjectural witness** for the Jones-polynomial framework.\n\nFields:\n- `markov_trace_existence`: `jonesAt` agrees with the Markov-trace\n  formulation `tr_M ∘ ρ_{n,q}` for any braid word.  Captures the\n  Jones 1985 theorem.\n\n- `skein_relation`: the Kauffman-bracket / Hecke-quadratic relation\n  on positive / negative / smoothed crossings.\n\n- `closed_form_*`: explicit Laurent values for the 4 canonical\n  knots in the probe (matches Murakami 1996 §1.4 conventions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.jonesAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.JonesPolynomial.jonesAt","kind":"opaque","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/JonesPolynomial.lean#L74-L85","doc":"The Jones polynomial of a braid word, evaluated as a real-valued\nfunction of the deformation parameter `q : ℝ`.\n\nDeclared `opaque` because the full definition needs Mathlib Markov-\ntrace primitives on `H_n(q)` (not yet formalised in this repo).  The\n`JonesPolynomialDef` class below pins the empirical closed forms\nused by the metallic-q probe.\n\nFor Lean-side rational arithmetic, the actual range is the Laurent\npolynomial ring `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`; we use `ℝ`-valued evaluation here so\nthat the metallic-piecewise conjecture can be stated over real q. ","signatureChunk":0}]}